  "prefLabel": "Rev 601.37 Partial update",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rev 601.37 “Partial update” means the process of analyzing market sales throughout the entire municipality to identify and implement needed value changes to the affected areas, or classes of property, to bring those properties to the municipality’s general level of assessment utilizing the existing base tax year and providing an addendum to the existing USPAP compliant report. The term includes “partial revaluation.”\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Rev 600) #10581, eff 5-1-14; ss by #13916, eff 3-28-24 (formerly Rev 601.38) (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Rev 600)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/rev600.html"
